title: Campaign
subtitle: Meetings, rallies and the unions: one campaign on a matter that reaches several groups at once.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: {! return !!Q.S && !!Q.polish_party_rules && PolishParty.partyReady(Q) && Q.S.chapter.status !== 'ended' !}
on-arrival: {!
// Card party.campaign (Z — 0.77, decisions of 8 X 2026): five campaigns on a matter, each over its own groups, through
// meetings, rallies and the unions; rallies before an election in the last three months before the vote. One option, 1 T;
// since Z — 0.79 (decision 2A of 14 X 2026) no R. The direction and the character of the party and the state of the country strengthen a campaign; they do not choose it.
// The card rests three months after use (Z — 0.76). Z — 0.80 (the user's note of 20 X 2026): no rallies on the card.
PolishParty.campaignView(Q);
!}

= Campaign

Meetings, rallies and the unions. A campaign costs nothing but this month's action and reaches several groups of voters at once. [+ pl_campaign_line +] [+ pl_campaign_press +]

- @eight_hours
- @prices
- @land
- @republic
- @unemployed
- @easy_discard

@eight_hours
title: In defence of the eight-hour day
subtitle: [+ pl_issue_eight_hours_effect +]
choose-if: {! return PolishParty.issueCampaignStatus(Q, 'eight_hours').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_issue_eight_hours_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.issueCampaign(Q, 'eight_hours');
!}
go-to: result

